  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on outcomes with probabilities less than 20% and applies a specific probability transformation to them. However, neither lottery has outcomes below 20% probability, so the reason would not discriminate between them. The individual, in contrast, focuses on the higher chance of getting any money (i.e., comparing 20% vs 25% as chances of winning something), which is about relatively small but not 'very small' probabilities. The individual does not mention adjusting low-probability events upward or treating rare outcomes as more important; instead, they emphasize preferring a higher chance of a gain, which aligns more with a 'maximize chance of winning' heuristic than with the specific weighting rule for sub-20% probabilities. There is no evidence of the specific cognitive transformation (increasing weights of <20% outcomes by 10 pp) being used. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
